# Implementation plans

Any future implementation plan MUST use RFC 2119 keywords for requirements.

The plan MUST include this sentence near the top:

> The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119.

Use those keywords sparingly and only for real requirements or prohibitions. Body text that is not a requirement MUST NOT be capitalized as a keyword. Implementation plans MUST be English.
